To compile the New Rock compiler, run

	cc -o stdlib.o -c stdlib.c
	cc -o rockc rockc.c stdlib.o

The New Rock compiler reads from argument one as the
New Rock source code file to compile and argument
two as the include path. The include path specifies
the directory to search for files imported using the
include keyword 

rockpkg is a small shell script designed to automate
the installation of New Rock programs - simply type

	./rockpkg demo.rockpkg

to install the demo program 
please note to change the install path in the 
script, as well as to install a Pebble VM and
Rock compiler globally as pblvm and rockc

yes, the script is very janky, but it works

